Linux or Unix-like:

  To compile laby, you need ocaml >= 4.10.0, lablgtk3 >= 3.1.0 and
  lablgtk3-sourceview3 >= 3.1.0).

  Execute the following commands in the archive's main directory:

    make
    ln -s ${PWD}/data ${HOME}/.config/laby

  If you want the program to produce some kind of absurd sounds, make
  sure the alsa "aplay" command is present on your system.

  Now to run laby type:

    ./laby


Windows:

  Native 64-bit Windows builds use opam 2.2 or newer with MinGW.

  Install Git and opam from PowerShell:

    winget install Git.Git OCaml.opam
    opam init

  Then create or select an OCaml 4.14 switch and build:

    opam switch create . 4.14.2
    .\build-windows.ps1
    .\run-windows.ps1

  The build script pins a locally patched lablgtk3 3.1.5 because that
  release uses Unix-sized serializer types that do not compile on Win64.

  See README.md for details. The launcher runs through "opam exec" so
  the GTK3 and GtkSourceView3 runtime DLLs are available on PATH.
